.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.\" Title
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TH omc-diff 1 "" "OpenModelica @OM_MANPAGE_VERSION@" "OpenModelica User Commands"
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH NAME
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
omc\-diff \- compare two files, tolerating small differences in the numbers
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B omc\-diff
.I epsilon
.I file_expected
.I file_actual
.br
.B omc\-diff
.B \-v1.4
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.B omc\-diff
compares
.I file_actual
against
.I file_expected
and reports the first difference.
.PP
Unlike
.BR diff (1),
it parses the numbers in the files: integers must be equal, while a real
number
.I a
matches the expected
.I e
if
.RI | a " \- " e "| <= " epsilon " * |" a "| + " epsilon .
Runs of spaces and tabs are treated as one. Both files must be text.
.PP
The OpenModelica testsuite compares its results with it.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH ARGUMENTS
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TP
.I epsilon
The tolerance for real numbers, between 0.0 and 1.0.
.TP
.I file_expected
The reference file, holding the results that are expected.
.TP
.I file_actual
The file to check against the reference.
.TP
.B \-v1.4
Print nothing and exit 0, so that a script can check that this version of
.B omc\-diff
is installed.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
.TP
.B 0
The files are equal within
.IR epsilon .
.TP
.B 1
The files differ.
.TP
.B 2
The arguments were wrong or a file could not be opened.
.
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" --------------------------------------------------------------------
.
Compare the output of a script against its reference, allowing a relative
difference of one part in a thousand:
.PP
.RS
.B omc\-diff 0.001 expected.txt actual.txt
.RE
.
